pe (batch_size, input_window, num_nodes, feature_dim)\n   - Output: predictions shape (batch_size, output_window, num_nodes, output_dim)\n   - Note: LibCity may not provide 14-day history by default - adapt as needed\n\n5. Register the model in `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/__init__.py`\n\n**Critical Adaptations:**\n- LSTTN expects dual inputs (short + long sequences), but LibCity provides single batch['X']\n- Consider extracting long context from batch history or using a sliding window approach\n- Preserve all model components (transformer, dilated conv, GraphWaveNet, fusion MLPs)\n- Use LibCity's scaler for inverse transforms\n- Handle adjacency matrix from data_feature.get('adj_mx')\n\n**Important Notes:**\n- Keep the core architecture intact\n- Adapt data loading, not model logic\n- Reference LibCity/libcity/model/abstract_traffic_state_model.py for interface requirements\n- Test that the model imports successfully after creation", 'subagent_type': 'model-adapter'}
