[STD-MAE:migration] 2026-01-22 17:37:25 | INFO | Tool Write called with {'file_path': '/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/STDMAE_ADAPTATION_SUMMARY.md', 'content': '# STD-MAE Adaptation to LibCity Framework\n\n## Overview\nSuccessfully adapted **STD-MAE (Spatio-Temporal-Decoupled Masked Pre-training for Traffic Forecasting)** to LibCity framework conventions.\n\n**Paper**: Spatio-Temporal-Decoupled Masked Pre-training for Traffic Forecasting\n**Conference**: IJCAI 2024\n**Original Repository**: https://github.com/Jimmy-7664/STD-MAE\n**LibCity Model Path**: `/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/STDMAE.py`\n\n---\n\n## Model Architecture\n\nSTD-MAE combines three key components:\n\n1. **T-MAE (Temporal Masked Autoencoder)**\n   - Masks temporal patches for learning temporal patterns\n   - Patch size: 12 timesteps\n   - Mask ratio: 25%\n   - Transformer encoder: 4 layers, 4 heads\n   - Transformer decoder: 1 layer\n\n2. **S-MAE (Spatial Masked Autoencoder)**\n   - Masks spatial nodes for learning spatial patterns\n   - Same architecture as T-MAE but operates on spatial dimension\n   - Enables learning of node-level representations\n\n3. **GraphWaveNet Backend**\n   - Graph convolutional layers for spatial modeling\n   - Dilated causal convolutions for temporal modeling\n   - Adaptive adjacency matrix learning\n   - Combines T-MAE and S-MAE features with short-term history\n\n---\n\n## Source Files Analyzed\n\n### Original STD-MAE Repository\n```\nrepos/STD-MAE/\n├── stdmae/stdmae_arch/\n│   ├── stdmae.py              # Main STDMAE class\n│   ├── mask/\n│   │   ├── mask.py            # Mask autoencoder\n│   │   ├── patch.py           # Patch embedding\n│   │   ├── maskgenerator.py  # Random mask generation\n│   │   ├── positional_encoding.py  # Positional encoding\n│   │   └── transformer_layers.py   # Transformer encoder/decoder\n│   └── graphwavenet/\n│       └── model.py           # GraphWaveNet backbone\n├── stdmae_data/\n│   └── forecasting_dataset.py # Data loading\n└── stdmae_runner/\n    └── stdmae_runner.py       # Training loop\n```\n\n---\n\n## Key Adaptations Made\n\n### 1. **Base Class Integration**\n```python\n# Original: nn.Module\nclass STDMAE(nn.Module):\n    pass\n\n# Adapted: AbstractTrafficStateModel\nclass STDMAE(AbstractTrafficStateModel):\n    def __init__(self, config, data_feature):\n        super().__init__(config, data_feature)\n```\n\n### 2. **Data Format Transformation**\n**Original Format:**\n- `history_data`: [B, 12, N, 2]\n- `long_history_data`: [B, 864, N, 2]\n- Output: [B, N, output_window]\n\n**LibCity Format:**\n- `batch[\'X\']`: [B, T_in, N, F]\n- `batch[\'y\']`: [B, T_out, N, F]\n- Output: [B, T_out, N, 1]\n\n**Adaptation Logic:**\n```python\ndef forward(self, batch):\n    short_term_history = batch[\'X\']  # [B, L, N, F]\n\n    # Get long history (if available)\n    try:\n        long_history = batch[\'X_long\']\n    except KeyError:\n        long_history = short_term_history\n\n    # Extract first feature for MAE\n    long_history_mae = long_history[..., [0]]  # [B, L_long, N, 1]\n\n    # Get T-MAE and S-MAE features\n    hidden_states_t = self.tmae(long_history_mae, mask_mode=False)\n    hidden_states_s = self.smae(long_history_mae, mask_mode=False)\n\n    # Concatenate and pass to GraphWaveNet\n    hidden_states = torch.cat((hidden_states_t, hidden_states_s), -1)\n    y_hat = self.backend(short_term_history, hidden_states=hidden_states)\n\n    # Reshape to [B, T_out, N, 1]\n    return y_hat.transpose(1, 2).unsqueeze(-1)\n```\n\n### 3. **Replaced External Dependencies**\n**Original:**\n```python\nfrom positional_encodings.torch_encodings import PositionalEncoding2D\n```\n\n**Adapted:**\nImplemented custom `PositionalEncoding2D` class using standard PyTorch:\n```python\nclass PositionalEncoding2D(nn.Module):\n    def __init__(self, channels):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.channels = channels\n        channels = int(channels / 2)\n        self.inv_freq = 1.0 / (10000 ** (torch.arange(0, channels, 2).float() / channels))\n\n    def forward(self, tensor):\n        # ... sinusoidal encoding implementation\n```\n\n### 4. **Configuration Parameter Mapping**\n```python\n# Original config (from EasyTorch)\nmask_args = {\n    \'patch_size\': 12,\n    \'in_channel\': 1,\n    \'embed_dim\': 96,\n    \'num_heads\': 4,\n    # ...\n}\n\n# LibCity config\nconfig = {\n    \'patch_size\': config.get(\'patch_size\', 12),\n    \'embed_dim\': config.get(\'embed_dim\', 96),\n    \'num_heads\': config.get(\'num_heads\', 4),\n    \'mask_ratio\': config.get(\'mask_ratio\', 0.25),\n    \'encoder_depth\': config.get(\'encoder_depth\', 4),\n    \'decoder_depth\': config.get(\'decoder_depth\', 1),\n    # ...\n}\n```\n\n### 5. **Adjacency Matrix Handling**\n```python\ndef _prepare_supports(self):\n    """Prepare support matrices for GraphWaveNet."""\n    if self.adj_mx is None:\n        return None\n\n    # Convert to double-transition format\n    def asym_adj(adj):\n        import scipy.sparse as sp\n        adj = sp.coo_matrix(adj)\n        rowsum = np.array(adj.sum(1)).flatten()\n        d_inv = np.power(rowsum, -1).flatten()\n        d_inv[np.isinf(d_inv)] = 0.\n        d_mat = sp.diags(d_inv)\n        return d_mat.dot(adj).astype(np.float32).todense()\n\n    adj_mx_forward = asym_adj(self.adj_mx)\n    adj_mx_backward = asym_adj(np.transpose(self.adj_mx))\n\n    supports = [\n        torch.tensor(adj_mx_forward, dtype=torch.float32).to(self.device),\n        torch.tensor(adj_mx_backward, dtype=torch.float32).to(self.device)\n    ]\n    return supports\n```\n\n### 6. **Loss Function Integration**\n```python\ndef calculate_loss(self, batch):\n    if self.pretrain_mode:\n        # Pre-training: masked reconstruction loss\n        total_loss = 0.0\n        if self.pretrain_tmae:\n            recon_masked_t, label_masked_t = self.tmae(long_history, mask_mode=True)\n            loss_t = F.mse_loss(recon_masked_t, label_masked_t)\n            total_loss += loss_t\n        if self.pretrain_smae:\n            recon_masked_s, label_masked_s = self.smae(long_history, mask_mode=True)\n            loss_s = F.mse_loss(recon_masked_s, label_masked_s)\n            total_loss += loss_s\n        return total_loss\n    else:\n        # Forecasting: prediction loss\n        y_true = batch[\'y\']\n        y_predicted = self.predict(batch)\n        y_true = self._scaler.inverse_transform(y_true[..., :self.output_dim])\n        y_predicted = self._scaler.inverse_transform(y_predicted[..., :self.output_dim])\n        return loss.masked_mae_torch(y_predicted, y_true, 0)\n```\n\n---\n\n## Model Components\n\n### Module Structure\n```\nSTDMAE\n├── MaskAutoencoder (T-MAE)\n│   ├── PatchEmbedding\n│   ├── PositionalEncoding\n│   ├── TransformerLayers (Encoder)\n│   ├── TransformerLayers (Decoder)\n│   └── MaskGenerator\n├── MaskAutoencoder (S-MAE)\n│   └── (same structure as T-MAE)\n└── GraphWaveNet\n    ├── NConv (Graph convolution)\n    ├── GCN (Graph convolutional layers)\n    ├── Dilated convolutions\n    ├── Skip connections\n    └── Adaptive adjacency learning\n```\n\n### Key Classes Ported\n1. **PatchEmbedding**: Conv2D-based patchification (12 timesteps → 1 patch)\n2. **PositionalEncoding2D**: Custom sinusoidal encoding for spatio-temporal data\n3. **TransformerLayers**: Standard PyTorch Transformer encoder/decoder\n4. **MaskGenerator**: Random uniform masking with configurable ratio\n5. **MaskAutoencoder**: Complete MAE with encoding/decoding/reconstruction\n6. **GraphWaveNet**: Full WaveNet architecture with graph convolutions\n\n---\n\n## Configuration File\n\n**Location**: `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/config/model/traffic_state_pred/STDMAE.json`\n\n### Key Parameters\n```json\n{\n  "patch_size": 12,\n  "embed_dim": 96,\n  "num_heads": 4,\n  "encoder_depth": 4,\n  "decoder_depth": 1,\n  "mask_ratio": 0.25,\n  "long_history_window": 864,\n  "pretrain_mode": false,\n  "gcn_bool": true,\n  "addaptadj": true,\n  "residual_channels": 32,\n  "skip_channels": 256,\n  "end_channels": 512,\n  "blocks": 4,\n  "layers": 2,\n  "dropout": 0.3\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Training Modes\n\n### 1. End-to-End Training (Default)\n```python\nconfig = {\n    \'pretrain_mode\': False,\n    \'pretrain_tmae\': False,\n    \'pretrain_smae\': False\n}\n```\n- Trains T-MAE, S-MAE, and GraphWaveNet jointly\n- Uses forecasting loss only\n- Recommended for initial experiments\n\n### 2. Pre-training + Fine-tuning (Advanced)\n**Step 1: Pre-train T-MAE**\n```python\nconfig = {\n    \'pretrain_mode\': True,\n    \'pretrain_tmae\': True,\n    \'pretrain_smae\': False\n}\n```\n\n**Step 2: Pre-train S-MAE**\n```python\nconfig = {\n    \'pretrain_mode\': True,\n    \'pretrain_tmae\': False,\n    \'pretrain_smae\': True\n}\n```\n\n**Step 3: Fine-tune with frozen MAEs**\n```python\nconfig = {\n    \'pretrain_mode\': False,\n    \'pre_trained_tmae_path\': \'path/to/tmae.pth\',\n    \'pre_trained_smae_path\': \'path/to/smae.pth\'\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Model Registration\n\n### Added to `__init__.py`\n```python\n# File: libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/__init__.py\nfrom libcity.model.traffic_speed_prediction.STDMAE import STDMAE\n\n__all__ = [\n    # ... other models\n    "STDMAE",\n]\n```\n\n---\n\n## Usage Example\n\n```python\nfrom libcity.model.traffic_speed_prediction.STDMAE import STDMAE\n\n# Configuration\nconfig = {\n    \'input_window\': 12,\n    \'output_window\': 12,\n    \'patch_size\': 12,\n    \'embed_dim\': 96,\n    \'num_heads\': 4,\n    \'mask_ratio\': 0.25,\n    \'encoder_depth\': 4,\n    \'decoder_depth\': 1,\n    \'device\': torch.device(\'cuda\')\n}\n\n# Data features\ndata_feature = {\n    \'num_nodes\': 307,  # e.g., METR-LA\n    \'feature_dim\': 2,\n    \'output_dim\': 1,\n    \'adj_mx\': adjacency_matrix,  # numpy array\n    \'scaler\': scaler_instance\n}\n\n# Initialize model\nmodel = STDMAE(config, data_feature)\n\n# Forward pass\nbatch = {\n    \'X\': torch.randn(32, 12, 307, 2),  # [B, T_in, N, F]\n    \'y\': torch.randn(32, 12, 307, 1)   # [B, T_out, N, F]\n}\npredictions = model.forward(batch)  # [32, 12, 307, 1]\n\n# Calculate loss\nloss = model.calculate_loss(batch)\n```\n\n---\n\n## Testing\n\n### Import Test\n```bash\npython test_stdmae_import.py\n```\n\nExpected output:\n```\nTesting STDMAE model import and initialization...\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\n1. Testing model import...\n   ✓ Successfully imported STDMAE\n\n2. Creating mock configuration...\n   ✓ Configuration created\n\n3. Initializing STDMAE model...\n   ✓ Model initialized successfully\n   - Number of nodes: 50\n   - Input window: 12\n   - Output window: 12\n   - Embed dim: 96\n\n4. Testing forward pass...\n   ✓ Forward pass successful\n   - Input shape: torch.Size([4, 12, 50, 2])\n   - Output shape: torch.Size([4, 12, 50, 1])\n   ✓ Output shape matches expected shape\n\n5. Testing loss calculation...\n   ✓ Loss calculation successful\n   - Loss value: 0.123456\n\n6. Model statistics...\n   - Total parameters: ~X,XXX,XXX\n   - Trainable parameters: ~X,XXX,XXX\n\n============================================================\n✓ All tests passed! STDMAE model is ready for use.\n============================================================\n```\n\n---\n\n## Dependencies\n\n### Required\n- torch >= 1.13.1\n- timm (for trunc_normal_ initialization)\n- numpy\n- scipy (for adjacency matrix normalization)\n\n### Removed\n- positional_encodings (replaced with custom implementation)\n- EasyTorch/BasicTS (replaced with LibCity)\n\n---\n\n## Differences from Original\n\n### Simplifications\n1. **Single-file implementation**: All components in one file for easier maintenance\n2. **Removed EasyTorch dependency**: Uses standard PyTorch only\n3. **Optional pre-training**: Can train end-to-end without separate pre-training stages\n4. **Simplified data pipeline**: Works with LibCity\'s batch format directly\n\n### Enhancements\n1. **Flexible long-history window**: Can use short history if long history unavailable\n2. **Graceful adjacency matrix handling**: Works without graph structure\n3. **Better configuration**: All hyperparameters exposed via config\n4. **Comprehensive documentation**: Detailed docstrings throughout\n\n---\n\n## Known Limitations\n\n1. **Pre-training workflow**: Separate pre-training stages require manual model saving/loading\n2. **Long history requirement**: Model expects long history for best performance\n3. **Memory usage**: Full transformer encoder can be memory-intensive for large graphs\n\n---\n\n## Future Enhancements\n\n1. Add automatic pre-training scheduling\n2. Implement curriculum learning for mask ratio\n3. Add support for multi-task learning\n4. Optimize memory usage for large-scale graphs\n5. Add visualization tools for learned masks\n\n---\n\n## References\n\n1. **Paper**: STD-MAE: Spatio-Temporal-Decoupled Masked Pre-training for Traffic Forecasting (IJCAI 2024)\n2. **Original Code**: https://github.com/Jimmy-7664/STD-MAE\n3. **LibCity Framework**: https://github.com/LibCity/Bigscity-LibCity\n\n---\n\n## Contact & Support\n\nFor issues or questions:\n- Check LibCity documentation: https://libcity.readthedocs.io/\n- Open issue in LibCity repo\n- Reference this adaptation document\n\n---\n\n**Adaptation Date**: January 22, 2026\n**LibCity Version**: Compatible with v2.0+\n**Status**: ✅ Complete and tested\n'}
