[RSTIB:migration] 2026-01-22 17:37:48 | INFO | Tool Write called with {'file_path': '/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/RSTIB_ADAPTATION.md', 'content': '# RSTIB Model Adaptation Documentation\n\n## Overview\nSuccessfully adapted the RSTIB (Robust Spatial-Temporal Information Bottleneck) model from the original repository to LibCity framework conventions.\n\n**Paper**: Information Bottleneck-guided MLPs for Robust Spatial-temporal Forecasting\n**Conference**: ICML 2025\n**Original Repository**: https://github.com/mchen644/RSTIB\n**Task Type**: Traffic Speed Prediction\n\n## Source Files\n- **Main Model**: `./repos/RSTIB/methods/student/RSTIB_MLP.py`\n- **MLP Component**: `./repos/RSTIB/methods/student/mlp.py`\n- **Training Engine**: `./repos/RSTIB/engine.py` (loss calculation reference)\n\n## Adapted Files\n- **Model File**: `/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/RSTIB.py`\n- **Config File**: `/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/config/model/traffic_state_pred/RSTIB.json`\n- **Registration**: Already registered in `__init__.py`\n\n## Key Adaptations\n\n### 1. Architecture Components Ported\n✅ **MultiLayerPerceptron** class with residual connections\n✅ **Time Series Embedding** layer (Conv2d)\n✅ **Spatial Embeddings** (learnable node parameters)\n✅ **Temporal Embeddings** (time-of-day and day-of-week)\n✅ **Information Bottleneck** mechanism with reparameterization\n✅ **MLP Encoder** layers (configurable depth)\n✅ **Regression Layer** for predictions\n✅ **Dynamic Node Embeddings** (DNE) support (optional)\n\n### 2. LibCity Convention Compliance\n\n#### Inheritance\n```python\nclass RSTIB(AbstractTrafficStateModel):\n```\n\n#### Required Methods\n- `__init__(self, config, data_feature)`: Initialize model with LibCity config\n- `forward(self, batch)`: Standard forward pass\n- `calculate_loss(self, batch)`: Complete loss calculation with IB regularization\n- `predict(self, batch)`: Multi-step prediction with optional averaging\n\n#### Data Format Handling\n- **Input**: `batch[\'X\']` of shape `[B, T_in, N, F]`\n- **Output**: `[B, T_out, N, output_dim]`\n- **Temporal Features**: Extracted from last dimensions of input\n- **Scaler**: Uses `self._scaler` for inverse transformation\n\n### 3. Loss Calculation\n\nThe adapted model includes comprehensive loss calculation from the original implementation:\n\n#### Loss Components:\n1. **Prediction Loss** (MAE-based):\n   - Simple MAE or difficulty-weighted MAE\n   - Noise injection for robustness (noise_y added to predictions)\n\n2. **Information Bottleneck Losses**:\n   - `loss_info`: KL divergence on encoding distribution (mu, std)\n   - `loss_info_y`: KL divergence on output distribution (mu_y, std_y)\n   - `loss_info_x`: KL divergence on reconstruction distribution (mu_x, std_x)\n\n3. **Total Loss Formula**:\n   ```python\n   total_loss = loss_reg / log(2) +\n                2 * info_beta * loss_info +\n                2 * info_beta * loss_info_y +\n                2 * info_beta * loss_info_x\n   ```\n\n### 4. Key Features\n\n#### Information Bottleneck Mechanism\n- Variational inference with reparameterization trick\n- Three levels of IB regularization (encoding, output, reconstruction)\n- Gaussian noise injection for robustness\n- Multiple sampling support during inference\n\n#### Embeddings\n- **Node embeddings**: Learnable spatial features\n- **Time-of-day embeddings**: Captures daily patterns (288 time slots for 5-min intervals)\n- **Day-of-week embeddings**: Captures weekly patterns (7 days)\n- **Dynamic Node Embeddings** (optional): Time-dependent node features\n\n#### Architecture Flexibility\n- Configurable number of MLP layers\n- Configurable embedding dimensions\n- Optional features (spatial, temporal, DNE)\n- Multiple sampling strategies\n\n## Configuration Parameters\n\n### Model Architecture\n```json\n{\n  "input_dim": 1,              // Traffic feature dimension (e.g., speed only)\n  "embed_dim": 64,             // Time series embedding dimension\n  "num_layer": 3,              // Number of MLP encoder layers\n  "node_dim": 64,              // Spatial embedding dimension\n  "temp_dim_tid": 64,          // Time-in-day embedding dimension\n  "temp_dim_diw": 64,          // Day-in-week embedding dimension\n}\n```\n\n### Feature Flags\n```json\n{\n  "if_spatial": true,          // Use spatial node embeddings\n  "if_time_in_day": true,      // Use time-of-day embeddings\n  "if_day_in_week": true,      // Use day-of-week embeddings\n  "if_dne": false,             // Use dynamic node embeddings (experimental)\n}\n```\n\n### Information Bottleneck\n```json\n{\n  "info_beta": 0.001,          // IB regularization weight (beta)\n  "n_sample": 1,               // Number of samples during training\n  "n_sample_avg": 12,          // Number of samples during inference (averaging)\n  "use_ib_loss": true,         // Enable IB regularization losses\n  "use_difficulty_weighting": false  // Enable difficulty-based weighting\n}\n```\n\n### Dynamic Node Embeddings (if if_dne=true)\n```json\n{\n  "mid_dim": 64,               // DNE intermediate dimension\n  "dne_act": "softmax"         // DNE activation: softmax/relu/sigmoid/leakyrelu/softplus/none\n}\n```\n\n### Training Configuration\n```json\n{\n  "max_epoch": 300,\n  "learning_rate": 0.002,\n  "lr_decay": true,\n  "lr_decay_ratio": 0.5,\n  "steps": [1, 20, 50, 75, 100, 150, 200],\n  "lr_scheduler": "multisteplr",\n  "clip_grad_norm": false,\n  "max_grad_norm": 5,\n  "use_early_stop": true,\n  "patience": 20\n}\n```\n\n## Key Changes from Original\n\n### Simplifications\n1. **Teacher-Student Framework**: Removed knowledge distillation components (teacher model) for initial version\n2. **Beta Annealing**: Removed beta annealing schedule (uses fixed info_beta)\n3. **Difficulty Weighting**: Made optional via config flag (default: disabled for simplicity)\n\n### Enhancements\n1. **LibCity Integration**: Full compatibility with LibCity data pipeline and evaluation\n2. **Flexible Configuration**: All hyperparameters configurable via JSON\n3. **Logging**: Integrated with LibCity logging system\n4. **Documentation**: Comprehensive inline documentation\n\n### Data Handling\n1. **Batch Format**: Adapted to LibCity\'s batch dictionary format\n2. **Temporal Features**: Automatic extraction from input tensor\n3. **Scaler Integration**: Uses LibCity\'s data scaler for normalization\n\n## Usage Example\n\n```python\n# Load model through LibCity\nfrom libcity.config import ConfigParser\nfrom libcity.data import get_dataset\nfrom libcity.model import get_model\n\nconfig = ConfigParser(\n    task=\'traffic_state_pred\',\n    model=\'RSTIB\',\n    dataset=\'METR_LA\'\n)\n\ndataset = get_dataset(config)\nmodel = get_model(config, dataset.get_data_feature())\n\n# Model is ready for training with LibCity executor\n```\n\n## Testing and Validation\n\n### Import Test\n```python\nfrom libcity.model.traffic_speed_prediction.RSTIB import RSTIB\nprint("RSTIB imported successfully!")\n```\n\n### Expected Behavior\n- Model initializes without errors\n- Forward pass produces correct output shape\n- Loss calculation includes IB regularization\n- Prediction averaging works during evaluation\n\n## Performance Notes\n\n### Original Paper Results (PEMS04 dataset)\n- Uses information bottleneck for robustness\n- MLP-based architecture (efficient compared to GNNs)\n- Competitive with state-of-the-art GNN models\n\n### LibCity Implementation\n- Full IB mechanism preserved\n- All loss components implemented\n- Ready for benchmarking against other LibCity models\n\n## Limitations and Future Work\n\n### Current Limitations\n1. **Teacher Model**: Knowledge distillation not implemented (can be added as extension)\n2. **Beta Annealing**: Fixed beta weight (original uses annealing schedule)\n3. **In-Out Degree**: Not implemented (original has optional in/out degree embeddings)\n\n### Potential Extensions\n1. Add beta annealing schedule via custom trainer\n2. Implement teacher-student framework\n3. Add support for in-degree/out-degree node features\n4. Optimize memory usage for large-scale graphs\n\n## Dependencies\n- PyTorch (torch, torch.nn, torch.nn.functional)\n- LibCity framework (abstract_traffic_state_model, loss utilities)\n- Python 3.7+\n\n## File Locations (Absolute Paths)\n- **Model**: `/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/RSTIB.py`\n- **Config**: `/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/config/model/traffic_state_pred/RSTIB.json`\n- **Source**: `/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/repos/RSTIB/`\n\n## Verification Status\n✅ Model file created and updated\n✅ Configuration file updated with new parameters\n✅ Model registered in `__init__.py`\n✅ Inherits from AbstractTrafficStateModel\n✅ All required methods implemented\n✅ Loss calculation includes IB regularization\n✅ Compatible with LibCity data format\n✅ Comprehensive inline documentation\n\n## Contact and References\n- **Original Paper Authors**: Chen et al., ICML 2025\n- **Original Repository**: https://github.com/mchen644/RSTIB\n- **LibCity Framework**: https://github.com/LibCity/Bigscity-LibCity\n'}
