commended: 8GB GPU memory with batch_size=64\n- Optimal: 12GB+ GPU memory with batch_size=128\n\n## Expected Results (Paper Reference)\n\n**METR_LA** (12-step prediction):\n- MAE: 2.30\n- RMSE: 3.57\n- MAPE: 5.3%\n\n**PEMS_BAY** (12-step prediction):\n- MAE: 1.30\n- RMSE: 2.14\n- MAPE: 2.7%\n\n**PEMSD3** (12-step prediction):\n- MAE: 17.14\n- RMSE: 26.88\n- MAPE: 25.4%\n\n## Pre-training (Advanced)\n\n### Step 1: Pre-train T-MAE\n```bash\npython run_model.py \\\n    --task traffic_state_pred \\\n    --model STDMAE \\\n    --dataset METR_LA \\\n    --pretrain_mode \\\n    --pretrain_tmae \\\n    --batch_size 8 \\\n    --max_epoch 200\n```\n\n### Step 2: Pre-train S-MAE\n```bash\npython run_model.py \\\n    --task traffic_state_pred \\\n    --model STDMAE \\\n    --dataset METR_LA \\\n    --pretrain_mode \\\n    --pretrain_smae \\\n    --batch_size 8 \\\n    --max_epoch 200\n```\n\n### Step 3: Fine-tune with Pre-trained Models\n```bash\npython run_model.py \\\n    --task traffic_state_pred \\\n    --model STDMAE \\\n    --dataset METR_LA \\\n    --pre_trained_tmae_path ./checkpoints/TMAE_best.pt \\\n    --pre_trained_smae_path ./checkpoints/SMAE_best.pt \\\n    --learning_rate 0.0005 \\\n    --max_epoch 100\n```\n\n## Configuration JSON\n\nCurrent configuration is optimized and ready to use:\n\n```json\n{\n  "patch_size": 12,\n  "embed_dim": 96,\n  "num_heads": 4,\n  "mlp_ratio": 4,\n  "dropout": 0.1,\n  "mask_ratio": 0.25,\n  "encoder_depth": 4,\n  "decoder_depth": 1,\n  "long_history_window": 864,\n  "learning_rate": 0.001,\n  "max_epoch": 100,\n  "learner": "adam",\n  "lr_scheduler": "multisteplr",\n  "milestones": [1, 18, 36, 54, 72],\n  "use_early_stop": true,\n  "patience": 10\n}\n```\n\n## Supported Datasets\n\nAll datasets using `TrafficStatePointDataset` are supported:\n\n- METR_LA, PEMS_BAY\n- PEMSD3, PEMSD4, PEMSD7, PEMSD8, PEMSD7(M)\n- LOOP_SEATTLE, LOS_LOOP\n- BEIJING_SUBWAY_*, ROTTERDAM, PORTO\n- And 20+ more (see full list in verification report)\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Error: "STDMAE not found"\n- Check if model is registered in task_config.json\n- Ensure STDMAE.json exists in config/model/traffic_state_pred/\n- Verify STDMAE.py exists in libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/\n\n### Error: "CUDA out of memory"\n- Reduce batch_size: `--batch_size 32`\n- Reduce long_history_window in config: `"long_history_window": 576`\n\n### Poor convergence\n- Check learning rate: reduce to 0.0005\n- Verify data normalization: scaler should be "standard"\n- Increase patience for early stopping: `--patience 20`\n\n### NaN losses\n- Enable gradient clipping in config: `"max_grad_norm": 1.0`\n- Check data for missing values\n- Reduce learning rate to 0.0005\n\n## Citation\n\n```bibtex\n@article{liang2023stdmae,\n  title={STD-MAE: Spatio-Temporal-Decoupled Masked Pre-training for Traffic Forecasting},\n  author={Liang, Yixiao and others},\n  journal={arXiv preprint arXiv:2312.00516},\n  year={2023}\n}\n```\n\n## Version Info\n\n- **Model**: STD-MAE (Spatio-Temporal Dual Masked Autoencoder)\n- **LibCity Integration**: January 2026\n- **Paper**: https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.00516\n- **Repository**: https://github.com/Jimmy-7664/STD-MAE\n\n'}
