[RSTIB:migration] 2026-01-22 17:58:43 | INFO | Tool Bash called with {'command': "cat > /home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/RSTIB_BUG_FIXES.md << 'EOFMARKER'\n# RSTIB Model - Critical Bug Fixes Required\n\n## Summary\n3 critical bugs prevent RSTIB from training. All are straightforward to fix.\n\n---\n\n## Bug #1: Tensor Shape Mismatch in Loss (CRITICAL)\n**Priority:** HIGH - Prevents loss calculation  \n**File:** `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/RSTIB.py`  \n**Lines:** 406-407\n\n### Current Code (WRONG):\n```python\ny_true_noisy = y_true_inv + noise_y.squeeze(-1).transpose(1, 2)\ny_predicted_noisy = y_predicted_inv + noise_y.squeeze(-1).transpose(1, 2)\n```\n\n### Fixed Code:\n```python\ny_true_noisy = y_true_inv + noise_y\ny_predicted_noisy = y_predicted_inv + noise_y\n```\n\n### Explanation:\n- `y_true_inv` shape: `[B, T, N, 1]`\n- `noise_y` shape: `[B, T, N, 1]` (already correct)\n- `noise_y.squeeze(-1).transpose(1, 2)` creates: `[B, N, T]` (WRONG!)\n- Simply use `noise_y` as-is for correct broadcasting\n\n---\n\n## Bug #2: Device Placement Error (CRITICAL)\n**Priority:** HIGH - Prevents GPU training  \n**File:** `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/RSTIB.py`  \n**Line:** 244\n\n### Current Code (WRONG):\n```python\neps = Variable(cuda(std.data.new(std.size()).normal_(), std.is_cuda)).to(self.device)\n```\n\n### Fixed Code:\n```python\neps = std.data.new(std.size()).normal_().to(self.device)\n```\n\n### Explanation:\n- The `cuda()` helper creates tensors on CUDA when `std.is_cuda=True`\n- But the model itself might be on CPU (device mismatch)\n- Direct `.to(self.device)` ensures correct device placement\n- Remove obsolete `Variable()` wrapper (no longer needed in modern PyTorch)\n\n---\n\n## Bug #3: Batch Key Check Error (MEDIUM)\n**Priority:** MEDIUM - Causes runtime error when DNE enabled  \n**File:** `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/RSTIB.py`  \n**Lines:** 298-300\n\n### Current Code (WRONG):\n```python\nif self.if_dne and 'te' in batch:\n    dne = self.construct_dne(batch['te'].type(torch.LongTensor))\n    node_emb.append(dne)\n```\n\n### Fixed Code:\n```python\nif self.if_dne:\n    try:\n        if hasattr(batch, 'data') and 'te' in batch.data:\n            dne = self.construct_dne(batch['te'].type(torch.LongTensor))\n            node_emb.append(dne)\n    except (KeyError, AttributeError):\n        pass  # DNE not available, skip\n```\n\n### Explanation:\n- LibCity's `Batch` class doesn't implement `__contains__`\n- Using `'te' in batch` treats the string as iterable and checks characters\n- Use explicit `batch.data` dictionary check with try/except for safety\n\n---\n\n## Testing After Fixes\n\nRun these commands to verify fixes:\n\n```bash\n# Test on CPU (faster)\ncd /home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/Bigscity-LibCity\npython run_model.py --task traffic_state_pred --model RSTIB \\\n    --dataset METR_LA --gpu false --max_epoch 1 --batch_size 8\n\n# Test on GPU\npython run_model.py --task traffic_state_pred --model RSTIB \\\n    --dataset METR_LA --gpu true --gpu_id 0 --max_epoch 1 --batch_size 8\n```\n\nExpected output:\n- No errors during forward pass\n- Loss values printed for each batch\n- Training completes 1 epoch successfully\n\n---\n\n## Estimated Fix Time\n- **15-30 minutes** to apply all fixes\n- **5-10 minutes** to test and verify\n\n## Risk Assessment\n- **LOW RISK** - All fixes are isolated to RSTIB model only\n- No changes to LibCity framework required\n- Fixes align with PyTorch best practices\nEOFMARKER\ncat /home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/RSTIB_BUG_FIXES.md\n", 'description': 'Create bug fix summary document'}
